Verdict
-------
PR #94 is applicable and reasonable. It is a complete browser-chat feature,
not a scaffold. Users save named profiles: MCP allowlist + optional system-
prompt override. Default (no profile_id) keeps today's behaviour (all tools).
Empty allowed_tools skips MCP discovery. Prompt order: profile > conversation >
DEFAULT_SYSTEM_PROMPT. Owner-scoped CRUD; foreign profile_id on /api/chat/stream/
is 404 before a conversation is created. The orchestrator filters advertised
tools and refuses off-list tools/call (runtime enforcement, not discovery-only).
Do not add an MCP gateway product. Harden only; do not rewrite.

Non-goals
--------
- Rewrite Chat Profiles
- Apply profiles to Jupyter / /api/chat/mcp-tools/ / /mcp-call/
- Merge PRs #90–#93 into this branch
- Fuse.js, admin "lock Default", Jupyter profile plumbing
- Open public ports, live Docker rebuild, /data writes, sudo
- Merge or deploy

Integrity vs other PRs
-----------------------
- #90 / #91: no file overlap.
- #93: also edits header.tsx (Nodes menu). Different hunk from #94 Settings
  item; likely auto-merges.
- #92: will conflict on header.tsx and TabManager.tsx (both add a Settings
  item + route). After both land, Default chat can see secret MCP tools. Do not
  rewrite #92. One sentence in Chat Profiles docs is enough.

Live UI baseline
